  "outputParity": {
    "description": "Phase 9 P1: full leaf-path coverage across runtime JS, generated TypeScript, CSS, and DTCG, derived from the token tree rather than a curated sample.",
    "js": {
      "namespaces": [
        "colors", "space", "layout", "radii", "typography", "font", "shadows",
        "breakpoints", "zIndex", "transitions", "animations", "opacity",
        "aspectRatios", "icons", "border", "accessibility", "buttons", "forms",
        "link", "surface", "text", "component", "modes"
      ]
    },
    "dtcg": {
      "namespaces": [
        "colors", "space", "layout", "radii", "typography", "font", "shadows",
        "breakpoints", "zIndex", "transitions", "animations", "opacity",
        "aspectRatios", "icons", "border", "accessibility", "buttons", "forms",
        "link", "surface", "text", "component"
      ]
    },
    "css": {
      "description": "Each group declares the CSS variable prefix parts for every leaf under sourcePath, and a blockStrategy describing how the variable is expected to reach dark mode: 'cascade-only' groups are declared once in :root and MUST be absent from the dark block, reaching dark mode purely via CSS cascade inheritance; 'mode-scoped' groups are explicitly redeclared in both blocks with values independently sourced from modes.default.*/modes.dark.*; 'duplicated' groups are explicitly redeclared in both blocks with the same value in each, with no modes.* backing.",
      "groups": [
        { "sourcePath": "colors", "prefixParts": ["color"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "space", "prefixParts": ["space"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "radii", "prefixParts": ["radius"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "shadows", "prefixParts": ["shadow"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "breakpoints", "prefixParts": ["breakpoint"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "zIndex", "prefixParts": ["z-index"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "opacity", "prefixParts": ["opacity"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "icons", "prefixParts": ["icon"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "aspectRatios", "prefixParts": ["aspect-ratio"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "border.width", "prefixParts": ["border", "width"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "border.style", "prefixParts": ["border", "style"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "transitions.duration", "prefixParts": ["duration"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "transitions.easing", "prefixParts": ["easing"], "blockStrategy": "cascade-only" },
        { "sourcePath": "link", "prefixParts": ["link"], "blockStrategy": "duplicated" },
        { "sourcePath": "modes.default.surface", "prefixParts": ["surface"], "blockStrategy": "mode-scoped" },
        { "sourcePath": "modes.default.text.onPage", "prefixParts": ["text", "on", "page"], "blockStrategy": "mode-scoped" },
        { "sourcePath": "modes.default.text.onSurface", "prefixParts": ["text", "on", "surface"], "blockStrategy": "mode-scoped" }
      ],
      "exceptions": [
        "typography and font describe the same font scale via two parallel key shapes (fontSize/lineHeight/fontWeight vs size/lineHeight/weight/letterSpacing); css.ts emits from whichever is populated. Covered by check:css requiredVariables, not a generic per-leaf walk.",
        "layout emits per-branch (section.padding, section.gap, stack.gap, container.paddingInline, container.maxWidth/maxWidthProse, sidebar.width) with no shared prefix across the namespace. Covered by check:css requiredVariables and manifest spaceLinkedLayoutPaths.",
        "accessibility fields (focusRing.width/offset/style, minTouchTarget, minTextSize, reducedMotion, forcedColors) each have an independent CSS variable name with no shared prefix. Covered by check:css requiredVariables.",
        "buttons and forms nest by variant/state (buttons.primary.bg, forms.invalid.text) with irregular optional fields (border, shadow, focusRing only on some variants). Covered by check:css requiredVariables and existing button/form tests.",
        "animations splits into a flat set (fadeIn, fadeOut, ...) plus a nested reducedMotion sub-object emitted with an extra reduced-motion path segment. Covered by check:css requiredVariables.",
        "component is covered exhaustively by tests/css-semantic-coverage.test.ts, which already asserts full leaf coverage per component group.",
        "modes.dark.text is covered by the css-semantic-coverage test asserting tokens.modes.default.surface keys; dark-mode text/surface parity is asserted via requiredDarkModeVariables.",
        "typography.heading.* and typography.body map camelCase role fields (fontFamily, fontSize, lineHeight, fontWeight, letterSpacing) to distinct CSS suffixes (family, size, line-height, weight, letter-spacing) rather than the generic per-leaf checker's default kebab-of-field-name suffix. Covered by check:typography-refs, which is part of npm run check and asserts: every role field is a {typography.*} reference (not a bare scale/family string) that resolves to a real leaf, and generated CSS emits the fully resolved literal for every role variable with no dangling {} references and no var(--sp-font-*) indirection. tests/typography-roles.test.ts duplicates this CSS coverage as a Vitest suite for local dev feedback; it is not part of npm run check and is not the enforced gate."
      ]
    }
  },
  "protectedSemanticGroups": [
    "success",
    "warning",
    "danger",
    "cta-brand-action"
  ],
  "docContract": {
